Assistant: The best way to read a paper map depends a bit on the map and the situation, but generally you want to:

1.  Read the map from top to bottom, which will put the cities you want to see in the same order as they appear on the map;
2.  Try to figure out which way you’re facing on the map;
3.  If possible, use the map to orient yourself (in other words, make sure you’re facing north). This will eliminate any confusion over which way you’re looking and will allow you to read the map more easily.
4.  Once you’ve determined the order of the cities you’re interested in seeing, you can use the map to find their locations on the map.

